//! task: write
//! ask: Fold the text "I" to lowercase without needing any capability.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §5.1
//! explain: Locale-free case folding is total and needs no capability: `"I".plica_unicode()` is always `"i"`. The locale-dependent variant, `plica_sermone(sermo)`, takes the `sermo` capability as an argument. `[OPEN]`: text methods type-check but the lowering cannot emit them yet, so this is checked and not run.

publica functio f() -> textus {
    redde "I".plica_unicode();
}
